<%#
  A suggestion list, with each option's folded form attached.

  Renders only the <datalist>, not the field, because the author row repeats:
  several inputs share one list, and the inputs themselves differ too much
  between pages (labels, maxlength, validation state) to be worth centralising.
  A field opts in by carrying list="<id>" and data-suggest.

  The native <datalist> is deliberate and stays. With no scripting it is what a
  librarian gets — matching only on the literal accented text, but working.

  data-fold is the same folding the catalogue search uses, computed by the
  server so the browser never has to fold the option text itself. The browser
  folds only what is typed. See src/lib/normalize.js.

  Accepts options as plain strings, or as { value, extra } where extra is a
  second thing to fill in once the option is chosen (a reader's class).
-%>
<datalist id="<%= id %>"
          data-suggest-none="<%= t('suggest.none') %>"
          data-suggest-count="<%= t('suggest.count', { n: '{n}' }) %>">
  <% options.forEach(function (option) { -%>
    <% const value = typeof option === 'string' ? option : option.value; -%>
    <% const extra = typeof option === 'string' ? '' : (option.extra || ''); -%>
    <option value="<%= value %>" data-fold="<%= fold(value) %>"<% if (extra) { %> data-extra="<%= extra %>" label="<%= extra %>"<% } %>></option>
  <% }); -%>
</datalist>
